WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,
everyone,

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.033
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.334
We are here tonight.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:06.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:08.000
You guys,
I'm very excited about this.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.901
The one and only Mariah Carey
is my guest here tonight.

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:15.100
That's right.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.434
We're kicking off the holiday
season on a very high note.

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:19.901
That's right.

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:21.767
By the way, you don't
just invite Mariah.

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:23.200
You have to say "Christmas"
three times

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.434
and she suddenly appears.

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:25.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:28.167
Yeah, Mariah has been dubbed
the Queen of Christmas,

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.534
which explains why Mrs. Claus
just tweeted this.

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:32.501
Oh, yeah.

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:37.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:38.801
And this is fun.

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:40.300
Mariah just released
her new children's book,

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.968
"The Christmas Princess."

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:43.100
Yeah.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.901
I'm happy for her,
but it stung

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:51.100
when my kids were like, "Now,
that's a children's book."

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.067
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:55.300
"Say da, da. Say da da."
Yeah.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.634
Well, it's going to be a fun
weekend here in New York City

00:00:57.634 --> 00:00:59.834
because this Sunday
is the New York City marathon.

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:02.968
It's this weekend.

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:06.534
Is anyone here
running the marathon?

00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:08.000
-Yeah!
-Yeah?

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.634
[ Applause ]

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:10.901
I'm sure
that won't be the last time

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:12.300
we hear you're running
the marathon.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:15.834
Good luck for you, by the way.
A little trivia for you.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:17.434
I heard that the fastest
marathon runners

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:20.667
can hit a top speed
of almost 13 miles an hour.

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:21.901
[ Audience murmurs ]

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:23.634
Then everyone
who drives a Kia Sportage

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:25.100
was like, "Big deal, so can we."

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:27.901
That's right,
people from all over the world

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:29.868
are competing in this marathon,
and it's very interesting --

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:32.667
the city is adding some new
obstacles along the route

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:35.767
to give runners the full
New York experience.

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:37.400
I'll show you what I mean.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.234
In Times Square...

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:45.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:46.901
Yeah.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.901
Down in Staten Island...

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:56.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:00.567
Over in Washington Square
Park...

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:07.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:10.400
At this point...

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:15.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:16.934
As they go up
near Central Park...

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.901
Right over here...

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:30.100
[ Applause ]

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.267
Very cheap.

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:32.367
Also at this point...

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:39.701
And finally,
once they finish the race...

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:45.234
There you go.

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:46.834
The runners will.

00:02:46.834 --> 00:02:49.734
Good luck to everyone
running the marathon.

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.734
Meanwhile,
early on Sunday morning,

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:54.000
Daylight Savings Time ends.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.300
So, you'll gain an hour.
That's right.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:58.701
That's right.

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:00.968
At 2:00 a.m.,
all the clocks turn back an hour

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:04.267
while every bartender
lets out an audible sigh.

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:06.000
Whew! [ Sighs ]

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.100
Well, let's get to some news.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.901
With midterms
just a few days away,

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:12.200
former President Trump is going
on a final campaign blitz.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.868
At a rally last night in Iowa,

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:16.667
Trump hinted that he's
going to run again in 2024,

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.067
but he did it in
a pretty odd way.

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:18.934
Watch this.

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:21.000
-I will very, very, very

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.133
probably do it again, okay?

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:25.000
Very, very, very probably.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:28.667
Very, very, very probably.

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:31.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.501
-[ As Trump ] It's like my
favorite book,

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:35.734
"The Very, Very, Very Probably
Hungry Caterpillar."

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:37.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:40.400
Very, very, very, very,
probably.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.901
[ Applause ]

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:43.968
[ Normal voice ]
It's also how Trump

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:45.100
recited his wedding vows.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.200
[ As Trump ] I very, very,
very probably do.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.434 --> 00:03:51.968
Some more news on the midterms.

00:03:51.968 --> 00:03:54.868
Oprah, who launched
Dr. Oz's career,

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:57.334
just endorsed his opponent,
John Fetterman.

00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:59.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:04.000
Apparently, this year, one of
Oprah's favorite things is...

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.234
betrayal.

00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:07.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:08.901
Yep, Oprah endorsed Fetterman,

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:11.167
which explains why Dr. Oz
just tweeted this.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:15.601
Speaking of Oz and Fetterman,

00:04:15.601 --> 00:04:17.100
during last night's
World Series game,

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.934
I don't know if you saw this,
I noticed that ads

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:21.234
for the two candidates
aired back-to-back.

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:23.334
And the timing was pretty great.
Check this out.

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:26.501
-Together, we'll stand up
to extremism on both sides

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:28.133
and bring balance to Washington.

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:30.133
I'm Dr. Oz.
I approve this message.

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:32.300
-Oz is a piece of [bleep]
in my opinion.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:36.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:45.067
-Dr. Oz was like,
"The proper medical term is

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:46.300
piece of stool sample."

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:47.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.901 --> 00:04:49.300
Well, a lot of people
are talking about this.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.767
Jeff Bezos
is thinking about buying

00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:51.934
the Washington Commanders.

00:04:51.934 --> 00:04:53.167
Did you see that? Yeah.

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:56.067
Well, yeah, this guy
might become an NFL owner.

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:57.934
So we decided
to ask some NFL players

00:04:57.934 --> 00:05:00.501
if they want to play for Bezos,
and here's what they said.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:02.934
First, Trevor Lawrence
from the Jaguars said...

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:08.634
And Brendan Schooler
from the Patriots said...

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:15.067
Next, Andrew Van Ginkel
from the Dolphins said...

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:21.667
Then Billy Price
from the Cardinals said...

00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:26.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.200
Next, Lane Johnson
from the Eagles said...

00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:38.133
Then Brian Hoyer
from the Patriots said...

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:45.567
And finally, Las Vegas Raiders
owner Mark Davis said...

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.334
Well, get this.

00:05:55.334 --> 00:05:58.234
The M.T.A. just released
a new subway bingo game

00:05:58.234 --> 00:06:01.167
to make riding the train
a fun experience.

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:02.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.634 --> 00:06:04.701
The M.T.A. said, "Well,
it's the least we could do."

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:06.234
And New Yorkers were like,
"Clearly."

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:08.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.200
Yep, the bingo card has things
like escalator, wooden bench,

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.000
and business man getting kicked
in the face by a break dancer.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.601
It's fun.

00:06:15.601 --> 00:06:17.000
Well, hey, I saw this
for the holidays,

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.667
Miller Lite is releasing
a pretty wild contraption.

00:06:19.667 --> 00:06:20.534
Take a look at this.

00:06:20.534 --> 00:06:21.901
-Beer brand Miller Lite

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:24.300
is releasing
a Christmas tree keg stand

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.534
this holiday season.

00:06:25.534 --> 00:06:27.400
Its fully functioning tree stand

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.100
is designed to fit around
a quarter-barrel keg.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:31.501
Its design makes it seem

00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:34.067
like beer is being poured
from the tree.

00:06:34.067 --> 00:06:36.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.167 --> 00:06:40.267
-♪ I'm dreaming
of a white trash Christmas ♪

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:41.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:43.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:43.734 --> 00:06:46.167
If you thought the Christmas
tree was lit before...

00:06:46.167 --> 00:06:47.133
Yeah.

00:06:47.133 --> 00:06:48.534
Kids will be like,
"I saw Mommy

00:06:48.534 --> 00:06:50.801
dragging Santa Claus
to the couch."

